{"Backup code validation during login has race condition where two concurrent login attempts with the same backup code can both pass the indexOf check before either update is committed": 0.9194517731666565, "resetState() does not clear backupCodes or revoke backupCodesUrl, so sensitive recovery codes and their Blob URL can remain in component memory after cancel/close instead of being cleaned up": 0.9567158222198486, "navigator.clipboard.writeText() called without awaiting or catching the returned promise, causing silent failures when clipboard API fails due to permissions, secure context issues, or browser incompatibility": 0.9902245402336121, "Backup code validation has replay vulnerability where if an update fails silently, the code remains in the array and can be used again": 0.747161328792572, "Setting backupCodes[index] = null then stringifying creates memory bloat as null codes remain in array but indexOf() fails to match them": 0.18371064960956573, "Missing test coverage for attempting to reuse a backup code after successful login": 0.41526100039482117, "Missing test coverage for concurrent login attempts with identical backup code": 0.08826814591884613, "Missing test coverage for partial failure scenarios where validation succeeds but DB update fails": 0.0775742381811142, "DisplayBackupCodes step lacks cancel button, trapping users who want to abandon 2FA setup after viewing backup codes": 0.648084282875061}